<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15316" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēgestĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		egero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a carrying out</i> or <i>off</i>, <i>an emptying</i>, <i>voiding</i>
			(post-Aug. and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cadaverum et ruderum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventris et urinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Tard. 5, 10</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">for which simply egestio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 44 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 5, 14, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">publicarum opum,</span>”
				<i>a wasting</i>, <i>squandering</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 8, 6, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
